17
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:15,160
But in any case, I want to uh just give a little quick rundown this week on this 15 milliwatt laser diode.

18
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:24,760
Now, once you get up into the powers of 15 milliwatt um with helium neon lasers, it gives you the capability of doing some very nice creative work.

19
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:28,920
Uh the 5 milliwatt helium neon lasers are great for the classroom.

20
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:31,320
They're great to start out with holography.

21
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:35,720
Um there's uh I know there's a ton of things that you can do with a five milliwatt.

22
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:47,800
Uh my first five milliwatt that I had, I was actually doing multiple color reflection holograms uh using triethanolamine on four by five inch Agva plates back in the early eighties.

23
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:50,840
So there's a lot of things you can do with a four by five.

24
00:02:50,840 --> 00:03:07,560
Uh the 15, when you get up into the tens and fifteen, especially the fifteens, uh I guess the most famous 15 milliwatt helium neon laser out there is the uh Spectrophysics Stabilite uh 124B, which I've uh also had in the mid-80s.

25
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:19,320
And I believe, I'm not absolutely certain, but I believe I may have paid like $4,900 uh for that stabilite when it was new from Spectrophysics with the uh tube uh the head and the power supply.

26
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:25,880
I'll have to go back and see if I can dig out that uh sales receipt for that because I think that goes back.

27
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:29,240
I think I got mine back in 84 or 85.

28
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:45,920
But there were a lot of uh very uh well-known holographic artists that were working around the uh 10, 12, 15 milliwatt range for many years and created beautiful, beautiful display uh artistic holograms using 15 milliwatts of power.

29
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:51,600
So it's it's very advantageous to us to be able to move up into these higher powers.

30
00:03:51,680 --> 00:04:11,440
Now I know some of the uh holograms that are done for conventions, uh the large holograms that you see out there are using 50 milliwatts, so it's going to be interesting to see what this 35 milliwatt does, and this is really going to get us into the uh ballpark range of doing some very uh uh large-scale work.

31
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:14,000
I want to run down the prices for this.

32
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:25,920
Now, the 15 millilit laser diode that I have is putting out six hundred and thirty-five nanometers, so we're very close to the six thirty-three line of uh helium neon laser.

33
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:32,000
Um I don't think it's absolutely necessary to work with six hundred and thirty-five.

34
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:44,160
Everyone, when we were talking very early on about laser diodes saying it'll be great to get down around six hundred and uh thirty-three nanometers, and we're as close to it as we can with these laser diodes.

35
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:55,120
But the holographic emulsions are sensitive to a number of different wavelengths, for instance, uh the BB plates from Germany, and maybe also the Slavage materials as well.

36
00:04:55,120 --> 00:05:02,080
Both have a spike in the response curve at 647 nanometers for krypton.

37
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:17,120
So whether you're working with a 635 nanometer diode or 650, uh 635 is going to put you two nanometers away from 633, 650 is going to put you three nanometers away from 647.

38
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:19,360
So you're in the ballpark for both of those.

39
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:24,560
The main difference, the main difference is what you're going to pay for the diode.

40
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:34,200
Now, this 15 millilit 635 nanometer diode was $550 assembled.

41
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:45,320
Now, the same amount of power, you're going to be able to do the same size holograms, you're going to get the same type of response for a 650 nanometer diode.

42
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:58,600
Let me run down some of these prices for you just to uh because I know someone's going to hear $550 and they're going to think, well, that's just putting us right back where we were before, where people couldn't afford the higher powered.

43
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:04,120
And $550 is a big chunk for some people, especially if you're doing this as an amateur or hobbyist.

44
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:05,320
That's a big chunk.

45
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:06,600
So let's take a look at this.

46
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:13,560
Now, say for instance that you want to put your own laser diode module together.

47
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:20,840
Here's what it's going to break down to for 15 milliwatts of power at 650 nanometers.

48
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:26,760
You're going to pay, and these are approximate prices, maybe a little bit more, a little bit less, but we're only looking at a few dollars.

49
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:33,400
We're not looking at hundreds, uh, maybe three dollars, five dollars, because they're all relatively the same price around.

50
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:39,240
You're going to pay $90 for the 650 nanometer diode.

51
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:43,640
That's the raw diode in the little brass housing.

52
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:44,920
These are tiny little things.

53
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:46,840
You have to be very careful working with them.

54
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:48,760
Always make sure you're grounded.

55
00:06:48,760 --> 00:06:54,520
The slightest uh touch of static on a raw diode will absolutely fry it.

56
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:58,280
Don't even think about five watt uh five uh volts or anything like that.

57
00:06:58,280 --> 00:07:03,000
You're just just you walking across the carpet and picking it up, you're gonna fry it.

58
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,000
So you have to be very careful if you're doing this.

59
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,480
I just wanted to put that in there.

60
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:10,200
$90 for the actual diode.

61
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:55,840
Now, on top of that, you're going to need a driver now the diode's going to have to be it's either soldered to the driver or some of the dryer drivers have little uh uh uh receptacles or what we call females uh that you can plug the male end of the diodes into right on the chip itself so that's going to run you 30 you're going to pay nine dollars for a colonnading lens to go into the housing excuse me and twenty dollars for the actual housing itself now add that up you've got 90 30 9 and 20 and you're going to pay $149 for a 15 milliwatt 650 nanometer diode.

62
00:07:55,840 --> 00:08:07,360
Now if you'd like to move up to 20 milliwatts at 650 nanometers you can put one together yourself by adding about $65 onto the $90.

63
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:10,240
I think it's $155 for the actual diode.

64
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:17,120
So you're looking at $214 for 20 milliatts at $150.

65
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:19,040
That's that's a nice piece too.

66
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:36,960
Now you can also get these assembled if you've got a little bit more cash to spend and I'm not selling these I'm just trying to give people an idea of uh of what we can do and at what price because I'm comparing this to the $550 that was paid for the $635 nanometer 15 milliwatt.

67
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:50,680
So you're comparing $149 to $150 and you're still getting the same amount of power and your emulsion is still going to be just as responsive because it has that spike right there at 647 nanometers for krypton.

68
00:08:50,680 --> 00:09:12,280
Now, if you want these already assembled, you're looking at uh let's see, I have it all written down here I'm I'm shooting this from the hip because, like I had said, it's almost midnight, and I don't want to go over too long with this, but uh assembled, you're looking at $185 for the 15 milliwatt 650, and you're looking at 245 dollars for the 20 milliwatt.

69
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:25,880
That means that diode module is going to come already assembled in the housing, the brass housing, it's going to have the colonnading lens, it's going to have the laser diode, it's going to have two pigtail wires coming out of it where you just hook a couple batteries up to it and run it.

70
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:31,480
Um I did not have any luck running it off of the power general power supply.

71
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:41,000
Now, I had someone send me an email saying that you know, but I think they misunderstood the web page that I put up, meaning that I was running it off of one of those drivers that you just plug into the wall.

72
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:56,680
No, this is a very high quality regulated switching DC power supply from Power General, and uh I did not get one image running uh that diode uh diode module off of that power supply.

73
00:09:56,680 --> 00:10:01,000
And I was just uh doing everything as normal.

74
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:08,760
Uh we think possibly that the AC current going into these uh into these power supplies has to be very, very clean.

75
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:14,680
So we're going to put a scope on the AC power here in the studio and find out if there's a lot of noise in there.

76
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:16,360
You can't have a lot of noise.

77
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:18,600
So it looks like the batteries are the best bet.

78
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:21,720
And I also picked something up that I'm experimenting with.

79
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:43,080
Now it's uh running at half price for 1999, and it provides up to 20 hours runtime for C Ds that use two AA batteries.

80
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:45,600
You can charge this up to 500 times.

81
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:48,080
So I've been using it and it looks pretty good.

82
00:10:48,240 --> 00:11:01,280
Um it'll put out uh I think I measured it at uh four point one eight volts when it was fully charged, and I just ran it until the diode actually uh just went out.

83
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:04,080
But you can charge it up to five hundred times.

84
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:09,440
So this may save you a lot of money uh on batteries as well.

85
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:15,040
And the number for that is twenty-three five oh five.

86
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:20,640
That's uh stock number twenty-three-five oh five portable CD power pack.

87
00:11:20,640 --> 00:11:27,520
And it uh it's actually a little lead acid battery, and it's the size of a C D case.

88
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,520
That's how that's the size, it's very thin.

89
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:32,640
If you've got a C D case sitting there, take a look at it.

90
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:35,120
This battery is the exact same size.

91
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:41,120
And uh I've been running the Infinite or 200 off of that, uh, with very good results so far.

92
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:42,640
